{start_of_verse: Intro}
[C]On top of Old [C]Smokey all [F]covered with [C]snow,
I [C]lost my true [C]lover for [F]courtin' so [C]slow
Now, [C]courtin' is a [Am]pleasure and [C]partin' is [Am]grief,
And a [C]false-hearted [C]lover is [F]worse than a [C]thief.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[*]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For a [C]thief will just [C]rob you and [F]take what you [C]save,
But a [C]false-hearted [C]lover will [F]lead you to your [C]grave.
And the [C]grave will [Am]decay you and [C]turn you to [Am]dust;
Not one [C]man in 10 [C]thousand a [F]poor girl can [C]trust.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[*]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
They'll [C]hug you and [C]kiss you and [F]tell you more [C]lies
Than [C]crossties on a [C]railroad or [F]stars in the [C]sky.
They'll [C]throw their arms [Am]around you and [C]give your heart [Am]ease,
But the [C]minute your [C]back's turned they [F]love whom they [C]please
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
[*]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Come [C]all you young [C]women take a [F]warnin' from [C]me
Never [C]place your [C]affections on a [F]green growin' [C]tree
The [C]leaves they will [Am]wither the [C]roots they will [Am]die
You'll [C]all be [C]forsaken and [F]never know [C]why
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Instrumental}
